<!--
The chrome every blog post wears, nested INSIDE the site `Layout`: the site
shell is already applied by the router's declaration, so this file adds only
what an article has and a docs page does not, and never repeats the document
(no <html>, no <head>, no header or footer).

Nesting is by ancestry, so the wrapping is `Layout(ArticleLayout(post))`:
declared on <Route path="blog"> in main.bsx, it reaches every discovered post
and nothing else.

For now the post body passes straight through; the article header (title,
byline, date) arrives with the page metadata work.
-->
<Slot/>
